From 8e1f194416f1ec0a88925e6ee47dedb11c09cddd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:46:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 083/148] hydra: USD implicit surfaces rendered, as fine meshes

Sphere, Cube, Cylinder, Cone, Capsule and Plane reached the delegate under their
own type, which it does not declare: they disappeared without a word. A scene
index registered for Cycles CPU and GPU turns them into meshes before the render
index - points, normals and topology generated by GeomUtil from their attributes,
oriented along their axis, the rest of the prim (transform, material, primvars)
left as is; a modified radius or axis asks for the mesh again.

Hydra's own (HdsiImplicitSurfaceSceneIndex) does the same work with ten segments
around a sphere: the polygon is inscribed, the sphere came out 16 % too small in
surface area, and subdividing it shrinks it further. Here 64 segments, smooth
normals, no subdivision.

tools/bench_implicit.py, on the repo side, compares the silhouette of each to the
one its attributes give: 6/6, to within 0.4 %.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
